      "issue": {
        "url": "https://github.com/uibcdf/pytest-receptor/issues/54",
        "title": "Distinct external tests with pathless node IDs collapse outcome counts",
        "issue_number": 54,
        "body": "Consumer: `uibcdf/sabueso#112`. Related: #39 (rerun target for external tests).\n\nObserved with Python 3.14.10, pytest 9.2.0 and editable pytest-receptor `1.2.3+2.ga02820f`; its runtime source is byte-identical to the published `1.2.3` tag.\n\nThree separate external modules defining the same `test_reader` function, selected with a config outside their tree, generate three call records but the same pathless node ID `::test_reader`. Two calls pass and the third intentionally fails. The final artifact reports collected=3, executed=1, failed=1, not_executed=2. The verdict is correctly INCOMPLETE, but distinct actual outcomes have collapsed.\n\nMinimal synthetic setup: put an empty `[pytest]` config in one directory. In a separate directory write `test_0.py` and `test_1.py`, each containing `def test_reader(): assert True`, and `test_2.py` containing `def test_reader(): assert False`. From the test directory run:\n\n```sh\npython -m pytest -c /path/to/config/pytest.ini --receptor=llm \\\n  --receptor-events=events.jsonl test_0.py test_1.py test_2.py\n```\n\nThe artifact contains three call-phase records and one unique node ID. A control adding `--rootdir=/path/to/tests` preserves three unique IDs and reports executed=3, passed=2, failed=1, not_executed=0. Exit status is 1 in both controls.\n\nSabueso now supplies that explicit root to its copied archive-lifetime controls; no provider code or scientific assertion was changed. This differs from #39's failure-location/rerun-selector fix.\n\nPlease review how the provider should account for distinct physical items with duplicate pathless node IDs: preserve an item identity using the collected file path, or diagnose the unsupported identity collision explicitly while preserving raw execution accounting. The aggregation-by-node-ID explanation is an inference; the three raw calls and collapsed final counts are directly observed. All reproduction inputs are public synthetic code.\n",
